body:
In 4.3, *right-click* was erasing the tiles. The main issue of 4.3 is that the tools were not easily discoverable and they relied on left/right/middle clicks and modifier keys, which were conflicting with other shortcuts in Godot (e.g. right-click for free look navigation, or the modifier keys to emulate midle mouse button). 

In 4.4, all the tools have a discoverable button in the UI and a shortcut. You can switch between painting and erase mode with E and W. If you keep your fingers on the QWER row, it is still pretty quick to erase and paint.

@dpnnl to not be able to erase with right-click may be annoying to you, but not to be able to navigate the level with freelook or with a two button mouse (e.g. pen tablets) was annoying to others. However, I see your point, and I think we could add a setting in the grimap settings to activate "erase with right click", which will be off by default, so that freelook works by default. We could also expose a "Erase Action" in the Editor Settings shortcut, that the user can bind to any shortcut.

@Calinou at the time I was rewriting the Gridmap UI, it seems that freelock was binded by default on right-click; hence, my PR was solving the issue of not being able to use Freelook with gridmap:
https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/10405#issuecomment-2335153471

If you are happy with the solution I suggest, we can write a proposal 👍 .
